    "final_answer": "Upgraded `settlement_reconcile.py` to the v2 API.\n\nChanges made:\n- Switched from `/v1/graphql` to `/v2/graphql`.\n- Replaced the single unpaged query with a `SettlementConnection` pagination loop using `first`/`after`.\n- Stops only when `pageInfo.hasNextPage` is false, so short and empty pages continue correctly.\n- De-duplicates by settlement `id`, keeping the last delivered version for amended settlements.\n- Restarts from the beginning without `after` when a cursor is malformed or expired.\n- Retries `429 Too Many Requests` using `Retry-After`, resending the identical request including the same `after` cursor.\n- Writes output only after the full traversal succeeds.\n\nVerification against `http://the VM's public address:18081`:\n- Produced `1873` settlements, all IDs unique.\n- Compared every settlement to the v1 API output: `1873` exact matches, no missing/extra IDs, no value differences.\n- Also tested empty pages, amended duplicates, cursor restart, and 429 retry behavior with a local fault-injecting server.",
